    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "547:5",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Zoo",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Zoo"
        },
        {
          "text": "A Day at the Zoo\n\nLast Saturday, our school organised a trip to the city zoo. We arrived early in the morning when the zoo had just opened its gates.\n\nFirst, we visited the reptile house. Inside, it was warm and humid. We saw snakes, lizards, and a huge crocodile lying still behind the glass. The zookeeper explained that reptiles are cold-blooded, which means they need warmth from their surroundings to stay active.\n\nNext, we walked through the African savanna section. There were giraffes eating leaves from tall trees, zebras standing in groups, and elephants spraying water with their trunks. A baby elephant was playing near its mother, and everyone stopped to take photos.\n\nAfter lunch at the picnic area, we visited the aquarium. Colourful tropical fish swam in large tanks, and there was a tunnel where sharks and rays glided above us. It felt like being underwater.\n\nThe last stop was the bird aviary, an enormous netted enclosure where parrots, toucans, and flamingos flew freely. A guide told us that some of the birds were part of a breeding programme to protect endangered species.\n\nBefore leaving, we stopped at the gift shop. I bought a small stuffed penguin as a souvenir. The trip taught me a lot about wildlife conservation and why zoos play an important role in protecting animals.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "A Day at the Zoo Last Saturday, our school organised a trip to the city zoo. We arrived early in the morning when the zoo had just opened its gates. First, we visited the reptile house. Inside, it was warm and humid. We saw snakes, lizards, and a huge crocodile lying still behind the glass. The zookeeper explained that reptiles are cold-blooded, which means they need warmth from their surroundings to stay active. Next, we walked through the African savanna section. There were giraffes eating leaves from tall trees, zebras standing in groups, and elephants spraying water with their trunks. A baby elephant was playing near its mother, and everyone stopped to take photos. After lunch at the picnic area, we visited the aquarium. Colourful tropical fish swam in large tanks, and there was a tunnel where sharks and rays glided above us. It felt like being underwater. The last stop was the bird aviary, an enormous netted enclosure where parrots, toucans, and flamingos flew freely. A guide told us that some of the birds were part of a breeding programme to protect endangered species. Before leaving, we stopped at the gift shop. I bought a small stuffed penguin as a souvenir. The trip taught me a lot about wildlife conservation and why zoos play an important role in protecting animals."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. Why was the reptile house warm and humid?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. Why was the reptile house warm and humid?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. What were the elephants doing in the savanna section?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. What were the elephants doing in the savanna section?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What made the aquarium tunnel feel like being underwater?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What made the aquarium tunnel feel like being underwater?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. What is the purpose of the breeding programme?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. What is the purpose of the breeding programme?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. What did the narrator learn from the zoo trip?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. What did the narrator learn from the zoo trip?"
        }
      ]
    },
